   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to terms and conditions of employment of certain nonjudicial officers and employees of the unified court system",
    "basePrintNo": "S6494",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6494-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 42,
       "fullName": "John J. Bonacic",
       "imgName": "413_john_j._bonacic.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 413,
       "sessionMemberId": 1016,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "BONACIC"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Judiciary",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6494\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to terms and conditions of employment of certain\nnonjudicial officers and employees of the unified court system\n\nThis measure is being introduced at the request of the Judiciary. It\nimplements collective bargaining agreements between the State and\nseven (7) public employee unions negotiating on behalf of court\nemployees in the following collective negotiating units: Suffolk\ncounty; New York city administrative, librarian, clerical and support;\nNew York city administrative services; ninth judicial district;\ncitywide law assistants; New York city senior court attorneys; and New\nYork city court reporters negotiating units. These collective\nbargaining agreements provide salary increases and other benefits for\nthe period from April 1, 2016 through March 31, 2019.\n\nThis measure authorizes the following for affected nonjudicial\nofficers and employees during the period covered by the agreements:\n\n- Effective April 1, 2016, all employees shall receive an increment,\nif eligible therefor, and a pay increase of 2%.\n\n- Effective April 1, 2017, all employees shall receive an increment,\nif eligible therefor, and a pay increase of 2%.\n\n- Effective April 1, 2018, all employees shall receive an increment,\nif eligible therefor, and a pay increase of 2%.\n\nIn addition to authorizing the foregoing pay increases, this measure:\n\n- Provides for the payment of pensionable annual bonuses to affected\nemployees who have been continuously employed in the courts for 20\nyears or more, as follows:\n\n* If so employed for at least 20 years, $1,900 effective April 1,\n2016; $1,950 effective April 1, 2017; and $2,000 effective April 1,\n2018.\n\n* If so employed for at least 25 years but less than 30 years, $2,000\neffective April 1, 2016; $2,050 effective April 1, 2017; and $2,100\neffective April 1, 2018.\n\n* If so employed for at least 30 years, $2,100 effective April 1,\n2016; $2,150 effective April 1, 2017; and $2,200 effective April 1,\n2018.\n\n* If so employed for at least 30 years, $2,100 effective April 1,\n2016;\n\n- Provides for the payment of pensionable annual location pay for\ncertain affected employees, as follows:\n\n* For employees whose principal place of employment is in New York\nCity, Nassau County, Rockland County, Suffolk County or Westchester\nCounty, location pay at the annual rate applicable to such office or\nemployee on April 1, 2015, commencing April 1, 2016; $4,000 commencing\non April 1, 2018; $4,100 commencing October 1, 2018; and $4,200\ncommencing on March 31, 2019.\n\nWhere any of these employees already has received location pay during\nthe periods indicated pursuant to any other law, the amounts specified\nherein will be offset by those amounts received, except that no\nemployee who leaves service with the Unified Court System prior to the\ndate on which the Chief Administrative Judge and the employee\norganization representing the negotiating unit including his or her\nposition execute the memorandum of understanding including these\nprovisions for location pay (or, if unrepresented, the date on which\nthis measure becomes a law) shall be entitled to location pay under\nthis measure.\n\nProvides that, for all employees, increments and partial increments,\nlongevity increments and extra-longevity increments shall not be paid,\n1) unless an otherwise eligible employee shall have received other\nthan an unsatisfactory performance rating for his or her services\nduring the year immediately preceding, or 2) if as of the date on\nwhich this act becomes law, he or she already has received that bonus\npursuant to previous law.\n\nService in the employ of the Unified Court System is defined as\nservice in one or more courts or agencies of the Unified Court System,\nwhether as a judge or as a nonjudicial officer or employee.  The\nincrease in salary or compensation for officers and employees under\nthis act will be added to the salary or compensation of such officers\nand employees at the beginning of the payroll period the first day\nnearest to the effective date.\n\nThe changes in compensation set forth in this legislation shall not be\nimplemented until the Chief Administrator of the courts delivers to\nthe Comptroller a certificate that there is a written collective\nbargaining agreement with the State providing therefor.\n\nThis measure would take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have\nbeen in full force and effect retroactively as of April 1, 2016.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone. New proposal.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
